{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'diff -u POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md'","aggregated_output":"--- POSE.md\t2026-11-14 04:17:40.871677784 -0300\n+++ pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\t2026-11-14 04:17:40.914678106 -0300\n@@ -572,19 +572,6 @@\n - assisted execution via [`pose`](pose) (CLI)\n - progressive maturity with skills in [`.agents/skills/`](.agents/skills/)\n \n-## Open-Source POSE Contributor Mode\n-\n-<!-- pose:contributor-mode -->\n-\n-This repository has enabled POSE Contributor Mode. Executing AI agents collaborate on improving POSE engine stability and developer experience under explicit user adjudication.\n-\n-- **Continuous Opportunity Scouting**: On every issue resolution or task execution, proactively scout for related improvements, edge cases, root-level parity gaps, or complementary corrections across adjacent tools and commands.\n-- **User Consent & Explicit Adjudication**: Staging or submitting contributions upstream is ALWAYS an explicit user decision. Agents must ask the user for confirmation before staging drafts under `.pose/contributions/` or opening GitHub issues.\n-- **Lifecycle & Status Integrity**: Track contribution states (`staged` -> `submitted` / `dismissed`) with `pose contribute list --status <staged|submitted|dismissed|all>`, `pose contribute submit <file>`, `pose contribute mark-submitted <file> [--issue-url <url>]`, or `pose contribute dismiss <file>`.\n-- Check contributor status: `pose contribute status`\n-- Stage a contribution manually: `pose contribute stage --type <bug|enhancement> --title <title>`\n-- Disable contributor mode: `pose contribute disable`\n-- Privacy guarantee: staged reports strictly isolate POSE engine mechanics and never leak proprietary code.\n ## Opt-in progressive review profiles (ABM)\n \n Add `engineering-judgment@1` and/or `high-criticality-review@1` explicitly to\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'RoadmapCheck|roadmap-check|roadmap.terminal' pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy_test.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/closeout_review_policy_test.go POSE.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'RoadmapCheck|roadmap-check|roadmap.terminal' pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy_test.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/closeout_review_policy_test.go POSE.md\"","aggregated_output":"POSE.md:231:pose roadmap-check <slug> [--strict|--tolerant] [--json]\nPOSE.md:261:pose runtime run [--envelope] [--timeout <d>] <review-check|closeout-check|artifact-check|surface-check|roadmap-check> [args...]  # runs the check in the runtime when there is one, else standalone\nPOSE.md:380:- `surface-check` / `roadmap-check` — extend the same graph with typed `delivers` refs, production entrypoints, closed validation `evidenceClass` values and provenance-bound structured results. Surface profiles require reachability plus integration/e2e; composed capabilities require integration. Roadmap criteria may reference only registered delivery refs, checks or confined manual-review reports—raw commands are rejected. MCP: `pose_surface_assurance`.\nPOSE.md:954:**Hosted checks and the resident Git memo.** `pose runtime run [--envelope] [--timeout <d>] <command> [args...]` runs `review-check`, `closeout-check`, `artifact-check`, `surface-check` or `roadmap-check` in the runtime of the worktree when one is running, compatible and willing, and standalone in this process otherwise; the exit code and the output are the command's, and `--envelope` prints one document (`pose.runtime.run/1`) with them and with `via` (`runtime` or `standalone`), the `fallback_reason`, the typed `outcome` (`completed`; `error` when the command ran and ended but its output (over 2 MiB) is not sent back, with the command's exit code; or `unknown` for a deadline or a lost answer), the epoch and the memo hits. The runtime refuses, before the command starts, one it does not host and a caller whose environment digest (the `POSE_`, `HARNE8_`, `GIT_`, `CLAUDE` and `CODEX` variables, `XDG_STATE_HOME`, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` and `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`, the locale, `HOME`, `NO_COLOR` and the user) differs from its own, so the caller runs standalone; a command that reached the runtime and whose answer did not come back whole, or whose `--timeout` passed, may have run and is never repeated standalone unasked: it exits 1 and says so. The runtime runs hosted commands as the user that started it, in its worktree, with the output of a non-terminal, in the admission lanes described below; a command still waiting for its slot when its `--timeout` passes is refused, not started, so the caller runs it standalone. A runtime also keeps, between commands, the output of the Git reads that are pure functions of object ids or of the commit HEAD named when they ran, keyed by that commit and the shallow state (256 MiB, least recently used first; not for a linked worktree): the second `review-check` of this repository took about 10 s against about 25 s standalone, with the same output. The runtime admits hosted commands in two lanes, each with its own slots and a bounded queue: `short` (`surface-check`, about 10 ms on this repository) and `heavy` (the other hosted commands; `roadmap-check <slug>` takes minutes here), 2 and 1 slots by default and queues of 16 and 4; `pose runtime start|serve` take `--short-slots`, `--heavy-slots`, `--short-queue`, `--heavy-queue` and `--memo-mib` (default 256). A short query is not queued behind a heavy check, and a command that finds every slot of its lane busy and the queue full is refused before it waits and runs standalone. `status` and the handshake carry, per lane, `<lane>_slots`, `_queue_limit`, `_queued`, `_running`, `_admitted`, `_refused`, `_wait_ms_total` and `_wait_ms_max` in `metrics`. A measurement of the runtime on a real repository, with its thresholds fixed before the numbers, is `POSE_RUNTIME_MEASURE=<file> go test ./internal/cli -run TestMeasureTheRuntimeOnTheRealRepository`; its report is under `.pose/reports/`.\\n\\n**Review rounds.** The rounds of a scope are its sealed bundles that a completed delegated review concluded on, in the order those runs ended; `pose review verify`, `pose delegate ls` and `pose insights` show the round. From round 2, the generated brief (template `review-brief/2`; runs briefed with `review-brief/1` still verify) carries a `Previous round` section built from the ledger: every open finding with the identifier it keeps across rounds (`R<round>-<id>`), its severity, disposition and location, the previous run and its draft digest. The reviewer's draft is the fenced code block whose info string is `pose-draft`: JSON with `schema` `pose.review.draft/v1`, `decision` and `findings` (`id`, `severity` high|medium|low, `disposition` blocker|follow-up, `file`, `line`, `summary`), and from round 2 `prior_findings` (`id`, `status` fixed|partial|not-fixed|superseded, `evidence`) and `sweep`. A finding reported `partial` or `not-fixed` keeps its identifier in the next brief. A round-2-or-later draft that leaves an open finding unaccounted, calls one `fixed` without evidence or states no sweep is recorded with `draft_problems`, `wait` reports it as `invalid`, and it is never accepted as an approval. With `routing.rounds` `continue-thread` (the default) a round resumes the session the previous round ended with, through the agent's resume command; it opens a new session, recording why, when the agent or its vendor changes, the chain of drafts is broken, that session cannot be resumed, or the round reaches `routing.round_threshold` (5 by default), where `verify` also warns that the rounds are not converging. `cold-session` opens a new session every round. Each run records its `round` and `thread`; `pose insights` reports, per scope, findings per round, rounds to approval, and how prior findings were accounted for in continued and in cold rounds. A previous round whose record is not intact makes the brief refuse.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"python3 -c 'import subprocess,json; p=subprocess.run([\\\"pose\\\",\\\"artifact-check\\\",\\\"--spec\\\",\\\"pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit\\\",\\\"--strict\\\",\\\"--json\\\"],capture_output=True,text=True); print(\\\"exit\\\",p.returncode); d=json.loads(p.stdout); print(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in d.items() if k not in [\\\"findings\\\",\\\"claims\\\",\\\"observed\\\"]},ensure_ascii=False)[:4000]); print(\\\"finding_levels\\\",{level:sum(1 for f in d.get(\\\"findings\\\",[]) if f.get(\\\"severity\\\")==level) for level in [\\\"error\\\",\\\"warning\\\",\\\"info\\\"]}); print(\\\"first_findings\\\",json.dumps(d.get(\\\"findings\\\",[])[:2]))' \"","aggregated_output":"exit 0\n{\"schema_version\": 1, \"input_digest\": \"sha256:d9bb57b4db40833e947e22e835296e29f001e7024d00c4d9c16655760e628e27\", \"provenance_digest\": \"sha256:a5096eb51e0c8771fcb784abf957d965d827199cde55ef1e8461ebecd3166707\", \"nodes\": [{\"id\": \"artifact:.pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\", \"type\": \"artifact\", \"attributes\": {\"path\": \".pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\"}}, {\"id\": \"artifact:.pose/adr/2026-11-12-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-and-benefit.md\", \"type\": \"artifact\", \"attributes\": {\"path\": \".pose/adr/2026-11-12-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-and-benefit.md\"}}, {\"id\": \"artifact:.pose/adr/2026-11-14-governance-association-links-are-read-with-a-commonmark-parser.md\", \"type\": \"artifact\", \"attributes\": {\"path\": \".pose/adr/2026-11-14-governance-association-links-are-read-with-a-commonmark-parser.md\"}}, {\"id\": \"artifact:.pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md\", \"type\": \"artifact\", \"attributes\": {\"path\": \".pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md\"}}, {\"id\": \"artifact:.pose/closeo